{"title":"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_-_THE_MOST_TROLL_IMO_PROBLEM_IN_HISTORY_-_fast_solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 - THE MOST TROLL IMO PROBLEM IN HISTORY - fast solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution，中文版，subtitle_in_English,_5_mins_long\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution，中文版，subtitle in English, 5 mins long</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_(Strategy_Construction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution (Strategy Construction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Turbo the snail plays a game on a board with 2024 rows and 2023 columns.\nThere are hidden monsters in 2022 of the cells. Initially, Turbo does not know where any of\nthe monsters are, but he knows that there is exactly one monster in each row except the first\nrow and the last row, and that each column contains at most one monster.\n</p><p>Turbo makes a series of attempts to go from the first row to the last row. On each attempt, he\nchooses to start on any cell in the first row, then repeatedly moves to an adjacent cell sharing\na common side. (He is allowed to return to a previously visited cell.) If he reaches a cell\nwith a monster, his attempt ends and he is transported back to the first row to start a new\nattempt. The monsters do not move, and Turbo remembers whether or not each cell he has\nvisited contains a monster. If he reaches any cell in the last row, his attempt ends and the\ngame is over.\n</p><p>Determine the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which Turbo has a strategy that guarantees reaching\nthe last row on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> attempt or earlier, regardless of the locations of the monsters.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wfQkk9WktGE\">https://youtu.be/wfQkk9WktGE</a> (including commentary and some fun facts / backstory!)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1PAVmOboyTc\">https://youtu.be/1PAVmOboyTc</a> by Steakmath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_-_THE_MOST_TROLL_IMO_PROBLEM_IN_HISTORY_-_fast_solve\">Video Solution 3 - THE MOST TROLL IMO PROBLEM IN HISTORY - fast solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 - THE MOST TROLL IMO PROBLEM IN HISTORY - fast solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-E4Oab4DImg&amp;t=4s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-E4Oab4DImg&amp;t=4s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vxcEKbqr3h0\">https://youtu.be/vxcEKbqr3h0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.EF.BC.8C.E4.B8.AD.E6.96.87.E7.89.88.EF.BC.8Csubtitle_in_English.2C_5_mins_long\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution，中文版，subtitle_in_English,_5_mins_long\">Video Solution，中文版，subtitle in English, 5 mins long</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution，中文版，subtitle in English, 5 mins long\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-7s16_5No_g\">https://youtu.be/-7s16_5No_g</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Strategy_Construction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Strategy_Construction)\">Solution (Strategy Construction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (Strategy Construction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Our claim is that the minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies our condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We thus have two things to prove: that Turbo cannot absolutely guarantee success in either one or two attempts, and that there exists a strategy through which Turbo can absolutely guarantee a victory in at most three attempts.\n</p><p>Firstly, it is rather trivial that one attempt doesn't guarantee success for Turbo, as he doesn't initially know the location of the monsters. Now, suppose that, at the first attempt, Turbo hits a monster at row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. All he now knows is that, except the exact point he hit, the entire row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and entire column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> doesn't have any monster. So, the only optimal strategy left would be to walk along column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, as there is a possibility that each column holds a monster. However, since there is a monster at row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, at some point before approaching that row, Turbo would have to leave column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> by either shifting to left or right cell. However, there is no guarantee that the cell shifted to is monster-free, as that cell is neither in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> nor in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, the second attempt too doesn't guarantee victory.\n</p><p>Now, we construct a strategy for Turbo to guarantee victory in at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> attempts. Let the cell in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be called <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/7242cfa35ab9a2ca1a11f146a10c7cd6f2288d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />. Now, at the first attempt, Turbo traverses row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> until encountering a monster at, say, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb4227bc8ed3b342f4be4f169351636cdc70b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Then, he now knows that rest of the cells in row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are monster-free and also that column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is empty except at row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If this initial encounter cell is not at the edge of the board, then at the second attempt, Turbo can travel along the row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> till column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2924e05b65d0a1887d309cb3aad442e9ccee0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> and then shift to row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If the cell <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e1857ea33297846b5c50576d1640ccb9d715bf3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> is monster-free, then Turbo can simply switch to column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, travel along the entire column and finish the game at the second attempt. However, if the cell <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e1857ea33297846b5c50576d1640ccb9d715bf3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, c-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> is not monster-free, then Turbo knows that rest of row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is empty. Thus, at the third attempt, Turbo can simply travel along the row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> till column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a398005d35072ae993a9ac8b72dd8e746fcc416e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, glide along to row <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then switch to column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and then travel along the entire column to last row and certainly finish the game at the third attempt.\n</p><p>If instead, the initial encounter cell is at the edge, then the cell is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e5e775a9c75e811b355eab011630862f9d100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. Assuming without loss of generality that this cell is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, at the second attempt, Turbo can go to cell <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, then follow the sequence of moves repeatedly: shift to the immediate right cell, then shift to the cell immediately above. If, following this staircase pattern, Turbo finally reaches the last row without encounter with a monster, he finishes the game at the second attempt. But if Turbo instead encounters a monster, he may do so during an up move or a right move. If the encounter occurs upon making a right move, then at the third attempt, Turbo can follow the same staircase pattern till reaching the row in which the monster lies and, knowing that all the cells at the left are empty, he can travel directly to the cell of that row that lies in column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and then straight travel up the column to the last row and finish the game. If the encounter occurs upon making an upward move, Turbo can follow the same staircase pattern till he reaches the cell immediately to the south-west of the cell in which the monster encountered lies, and then he can, instead of making the usual right move, make a second upward move and then travel straight leftward to column <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and then finally travel up the column till he reaches the last row, thus finishing the game. Since all cases have been considered, this completes our proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO\" title=\"2024 IMO\">2024 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\nDocs link for solution from Mathismyfriend24 below\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12R9Re7aOdKWvyZN1Nwik79l-rBpmn9DcujWIhuyBpbw/edit?usp=sharing\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/12R9Re7aOdKWvyZN1Nwik79l-rBpmn9DcujWIhuyBpbw/edit?usp=sharing</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017133802\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 250/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6867/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.067      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.067      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28216:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017133802 and revision id 291156. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}